init.description:
{summary}

**How it fits together:** a **room** holds its lights, scenes, aircon, shades and what Room Off does. An **activity** (Watch Apple TV, Listen to music …) is what the room is doing: which devices switch on, which inputs they go to, and what the remote's buttons control while it runs.

Changes are kept here until you choose **Save and program the remote**.

sources.description:
**What happens when the activity starts:** every device switches on → the remote waits (the **wait** below) so they can wake up → then each device is sent to its input and the volume is set. A device already on the right input is left alone. Leave a field empty to leave that device as it is.

**Source:** {source}
**Volume device:** {volume}
**Also turned on:** {devices}

**Input missing** (e.g. Game)? A receiver often has several entities (Denon AVR, HEOS, Zone 2) — the inputs of all of them are listed, and the right one is used. Still missing? Type it exactly as Home Assistant shows it and press Enter.

**Turn off with:** for anything switched on by a button (IR projector, screen), pick its **off** button / script. Room Off uses it instead of the on-button. Leave empty for network devices and plugs — they switch off by themselves.
